#!/usr/bin/env bitcpy

[ Runs a turing machine ]
[
  A turing machine is described as a table of state transitions.
  Each state gets 2 bytes for what to do when encountering a 0 and another 2 bytes for 1.
  Each byte is of the form BMSS, where B and M must be either 0 or 1.
  (if they set more bits to 1, those bits will simply be ignored)
  B is what the bit at the current position will be set to.
  M is what direction to move to: 0 is right, 1 is left.
  SS is what to set the state to. Setting this to ff will halt the machine.

  There is a list of turing machines at the bottom of this file.
  Also check out the settings.
]
[
  Limitations:
  - The turing machine can have at most ff states
  - The tape has a length of 00001 bits, wrapping around on both ends
]
[
  This currently still has a lot of TODOs with the tracing functions,
  so with these settings you will simply get a single string being
  printed for every state transition. This string will contain information
  about what the state transition is doing in the future, but not right now.
  You can still use it to count the number of state transitions though.
  For example, running `bitcpy examples/turing_machine.bitcpy | wc -l`
  will print 21, because the 3 state busy beaver takes 21 steps to halt.
]



[ .00000000 ] 00010000 aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa

[ settings ]
[ .00100000 ] 08020000 30000000 [ address of state transition table and number of states ]
[ .04100000 ] 10000000 [ fd to write traces to ]
[ .06100000 ] 10000000 [ fd to write final tape to ]
[ .08100000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa
[ this will only perform a single read syscall,
  meaning the table must be written with a single write syscall ]
[ .0c100000 ] 0 [ read state table from stdin instead of specified pointer ]
[ .4c100000 ] 1 [ trace state transitions ]
[ .8c100000 ] 0 [ trace tape ] [ currently doesn't work ]
[ .cc100000 ] 0 [ print tape when halting ] [ currently doesn't work ]
[ .0d100000 ] aaaa aaaaaaaa
[ .00200000 ]


[
  .0000_0000 - .0008_0000  bitcpy program memory
  .0008_0000 - .0000_1000  turing machine program memory
  .0000_1000 - .0000_2000  turing machine tape memory
]


[ misc constants ]
[ .00200000 ] 00000000 00000000
[ .04200000 ] 10000000 10000000
[ .08200000 ] ffffffff
[ .0a200000 ] c3000000 [ exit syscall ]
[ .0c200000 ] 00080000
[ .0e200000 ] 00001000
[ .00300000 ] 25c4 [ "RL" string ]
[ .01300000 ] a3020302030302d2e302030203020303a000 [ ": 0 00 -> 0 0 00\n\0" string ]
[ .0a300000 ] 00200000 [ dumpmem syscall ]

[ lookup tables ]
[ .0c300000 ] fff7 [ != f ]
[ .0d300000 ] efff [ != 0 ]
[ .0e300000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .00400000 ] 12345678 9abcdef0 [ increment ]
[ .04400000 ] f0123456 789abcde [ decrement ]
[ .08400000 ] 01234567 89abcdef
[ .0c400000 ] fff7 [ increment overflow (0 on overflow) ]
[ .0d400000 ] efff [ decrement overflow (0 on overflow) ]
[ .0e400000 ] ffff0000 [ loop continuation ]
[ .00500000 ] 03132333 43536373 83931626 36465666 [ hex digit chars ]

[ turing machine state ]
[ When modifying the pointer, make sure to only modify the first 01 bits. ]
[ This way, if the pointer goes too far left or right, it will simply wrap ]
[ around to the other end, effectively giving a circular tape. ]
[ .08500000 ] 00081000 [ pointer to current bit in tape ]
[ .0a500000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0c500000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0e500000 ] 00 [ current state ]
[ .8e500000 ] 00 [ temporary place for bit at pointer ]
[ .0f500000 ] aaaa [ temporary copy of current state transition ]
[ .00600000 ] aaaaaaaa [ temporary copy of pointer ]
[ .02600000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .04600000 ] 


[ increment/decrement pointer function ]

[ .04600000 ] 00700000 [ call address (A) ]
[ .06600000 ] 0e710000 [ return address (already correct for main function) ]
[ .08600000 ] 00000000 [ 0: increment, 1: decrement ]
[ .0a600000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0c600000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0e600000 ] 00000000 [ i ]
[ .00700000 ] 02800000 [ start of loop (S) ]
[ .02700000 ] 00000000 [ current hex digit ]
[ .04700000 ] aaaaaaaa

[ .06700000 ] 08600000 60a00000 10000000 [ A: adjust inc/dec lookup pointer of L ]
[ .0c700000 ] 08600000 4ca00000 10000000 [    adjust inc/dec overflow lookup pointer of O ]
[ .02800000 ] 00200000 0e600000 02000000 [    i = 0 ]
[ .08800000 ] 0e600000 2e800000 20000000 [ S: current hex digit = digit at i ]
[ .0e800000 ] 08500000 02700000 40000000 [    current hex digit = digit at i ]
[ .04900000 ] 02700000 20a00000 40000000 [    write current to source of L ]
[ .0a900000 ] 0e600000 22a00000 20000000 [    write i to dest of L ]
[ .00a00000 ] 00400000 08500000 40000000 [ L: lookup inc/dec of current, write to pointer at i ]
[ .06a00000 ] 02700000 0ca00000 40000000 [    write current to source of O ]
[ .0ca00000 ] 0c400000 56b00000 10000000 [ O: write overflow lookup to R ]
[ .02b00000 ] 06600000 00000000 00000000 [ R: if not overflow (lookup has 1), jump to return ]
[ .08b00000 ] 0e600000 2eb00000 30000000 [    increment i ]
[ .0eb00000 ] 00400000 0e600000 30000000 [    increment i ]
[ .04c00000 ] 0e600000 2ac00000 30000000 [    write i to next instruction ]
[ .0ac00000 ] 0e400000 54d00000 10000000 [    lookup loop continuation, write to E ]
[ .00d00000 ] 00700000 00000000 00000000 [ E: if loop continuation is 1, jump to S ]
[ .06d00000 ] 06600000 00000000 02000000 [    return ]


[ .0cd00000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa



[ main function ]

[ .02e00000 ] 04210000 [ I ]
[ .04e00000 ] 0c310000 [ M ]
[ .06e00000 ] 0e710000 [ final trace tape return ]
[ .08e00000 ] 06310000 [ A ]
[ .0ae00000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0ce00000 ] aaaaaaaa
[ .0ee00000 ] aaaaaaaa

[ lookup table for != ff ]
[ .00f00000 ] ffffffff ffffffff ffffffff ffffffff ffffffff ffffffff ffffffff fffffff7

[ setup for running the machine ]
[ grow the memory ahead of time, so that it doesn't have to grow later ]
[ and write the state transition table to a standardized place ]
[ .00010000 ] 00200000 ffff1000 10000000 [    ensure that the memory has 00002 bits ]
[ .06010000 ] 0c100000 50110000 10000000 [    should this use stdin? ]
[ .0c010000 ] 02e00000 00000000 00000000 [    if so, jump to I ]
[ .02110000 ] 00100000 0e110000 02000000 [    copy table pointer to C ]
[ .08110000 ] 02100000 52210000 80000000 [    copy state count to C ]
[ .0e110000 ] aaaaaaaa 00080000 00000000 [ C: copy turing machine to correct place ]
[ .04210000 ] 08e00000 00000000 02000000 [    jump to A ]
[ .0a210000 ] 0c200000 06000000 02000000 [ I: set read ptr to 0008 ]
[ .00310000 ] 0c200000 08000000 02000000 [    set read len to 0008 ]
[ .06310000 ] 00200000 02000000 04000000 [    perform read syscall ]
[ .0c310000 ] 04100000 04000000 02000000 [ A: set fd for trace writing ]

[ actually running the machine]
[ .02410000 ] 08500000 08410000 01000000 [ M: read current bit ]
[ .08410000 ] aaaa1000 8e500000 10000000 [    write current bit to fixed location ]
[ .0e410000 ] 8e500000 4a510000 10000000 [    adjust source of W based on current bit ]
[ .04510000 ] 0e500000 5a510000 80000000 [    adjust source of W based on current state ]
[ .0a510000 ] 00080000 0f500000 01000000 [ W: write state transition to fixed location ]
[ .00610000 ] 4c100000 5a610000 10000000 [    should we trace state transitions? ]
[ .06610000 ] 0cc10000 00000000 00000000 [    if so, call trace state transition ]
[ .0c610000 ] 08500000 04710000 01000000 [    set address of B to tape pointer ]
[ .02710000 ] 0f500000 aaaa1000 10000000 [ B: write new bit to tape ]
[ .08710000 ] 4f500000 08600000 10000000 [    decide inc/dec based on R/L ]
[ .0e710000 ] 04600000 00000000 02000000 [    call inc/dec pointer ]
[ .04810000 ] 8f500000 0e500000 80000000 [    set new state ]
[ .0a810000 ] 8c100000 54910000 10000000 [    should we trace the tape? ]
[ .00910000 ] 0cd10000 00000000 00000000 [    if so, call trace tape ]
[ .06910000 ] 0e500000 0c910000 80000000 [    is state != ff? ]
[ .0c910000 ] 00f00000 56a10000 10000000 [    is state != ff? ]
[ .02a10000 ] 04e00000 00000000 00000000 [    if so, jump to M ]
[ .08a10000 ] 06100000 04000000 02000000 [    set final tape fd ]
[ .0ea10000 ] 06e00000 0ad10000 02000000 [    set return address of trace tape ]
[ .04b10000 ] cc100000 5eb10000 10000000 [    should we trace the final tape? ]
[ .0ab10000 ] 0cd10000 00000000 00000000 [    if so, call trace tape ]
[ .00c10000 ] 00200000 04000000 02000000 [    set exit status to 0 ]
[ .06c10000 ] 0a200000 02000000 02000000 [    do exit syscall ]




